1
00:04:07,500 --> 00:04:13,500
A romantic comedy. With zombies.

2
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:21,000
Shaun of the Dead is a horror, comedy film directed by Edgar Wright.

3
00:12:22,500 --> 00:12:28,500
Shaun lives a supremely uneventful life, which revolves around his
girlfriend, his mother, and, above all, his local pub.

4
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:36,000
This gentle routine is threatened when the dead return to life and
make strenuous attempts to snack on ordinary Londoners.

5
00:20:37,500 --> 00:20:43,500
Shaun, played by Simon Pegg.

6
00:24:45,000 --> 00:24:51,000
Ed, played by Nick Frost.

7
00:28:52,500 --> 00:28:58,500
Liz, played by Kate Ashfield.

8
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:06,000
Dianne, played by Lucy Davis.

9
00:37:07,500 --> 00:37:13,500
David, played by Dylan Moran.

10
00:41:15,000 --> 00:41:21,000
Yvonne, played by Jessica Hynes.

11
00:45:22,500 --> 00:45:28,500
Shaun of the Dead is a 2004 British zombie comedy film directed by
Edgar Wright and written by Wright and Simon Pegg.

12
00:49:30,000 --> 00:49:36,000
Pegg stars as Shaun, a downtrodden London salesman who is caught
alongside his loved ones in a zombie apocalypse.

13
00:53:37,500 --> 00:53:43,500
It also stars Nick Frost in his film debut, Kate Ashfield, Lucy
Davis, Dylan Moran, Bill Nighy, and Penelope Wilton.

14
00:57:45,000 --> 00:57:51,000
It is the first film in Wright and Pegg's Three Flavours Cornetto trilogy,
followed by Hot Fuzz (2007) and The World's End (2013).

15
01:01:52,500 --> 01:01:58,500
Shaun of the Dead was inspired by ideas Pegg and Wright used for their 1999–2001 television sitcom
Spaced, particularly an episode in which Pegg's character hallucinates a zombie invasion.

16
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
The film references the Night of the Living Dead films by George A.

17
01:10:07,500 --> 01:10:13,500
Principal photography took place across London and at Ealing
Studios for nine weeks between May and June 2003.

18
01:14:15,000 --> 01:14:21,000
Shaun of the Dead premiered in London on 29 March 2004, before it was theatrically released in
the United Kingdom on 9 April 2004 and in the United States on 24 September.

19
01:18:22,500 --> 01:18:28,500
It was met with critical acclaim and commercial success, grossing $38.7 million worldwide on a budget
of $6.1 million and receiving three nominations at the British Academy Film Awards.

20
01:22:30,000 --> 01:22:36,000
It was ranked third on the Channel 4 list of the 50 Greatest
Comedy Films and quickly acquired a cult following.

21
01:26:37,500 --> 01:26:43,500
In film studies, it is seen as a product of post-9/11 anxiety and a model for transnational comedy, while the
zombie outbreak as depicted in the film has been used as a modelling example for disease control.

22
01:30:45,000 --> 01:30:51,000
The film explores themes of london, england, dark
comedy, satire, surrey, parody.

23
01:34:52,500 --> 01:34:58,500
The tone is lighthearted and dark and intense.
